# Intro
A single, fixed-mass star at the center of a uniform, periodic glass-IC gas
box, with LW/FUV hyperbolic (Cattaneo/P1-relaxation) propagation on
(photoionization and radiation pressure off) and the Stage-1 triggered
artificial-dissipation term on (`GEARFeedback:LW_FUV_dissipation_alpha_max:
0.5`). Same pinned-neighbour IC family as the sibling `ISRFCausalReach`
example (one gas particle nearest the star set to a different initial
temperature, `T_hot = 3e4 K` by default here), which produces a sharp
local density/temperature contrast. Demonstrates that the dissipation
term eliminates negative `FUVSpecificEnergies`/`LWSpecificEnergies`
values that otherwise appear on that contrast, without degrading the
propagated field's causal reach (`r <= c_hyp*(t - t0)`).

## Dissipation term
`LW_FUV_dissipation_alpha_max` bounds a triggered artificial-conductivity
coefficient (Stage 1 of a staged scheme; see `parameter_example.yml` for
the full parameter description and
`src/feedback/GEAR/radiation_dissipation_stages.h` for the later stages,
both off here). It activates per-particle where a particle's own field
undershoots its neighbours' kernel-mean field
(`GEARFeedback:LW_FUV_dissipation_negativity_threshold`, code default),
and is bounded by the runtime stability check in `feedback_properties.h`:
`6.2*alpha_max*LW_FUV_c_hyp_margin + 0.70*LW_FUV_c_hyp_margin^2 <= 2`, so
`alpha_max` and `LW_FUV_c_hyp_margin` cannot both be changed independently
of that bound.

## Pinned-neighbour variant, metallicity, cooling
Same as `ISRFCausalReach`: see that example's README for the full
mechanism (`hot_particle_temperature_K`, `SPH:initial_temperature: 0`,
`isrf_dissipation_check.py --hot-particle-id`, metallicity/cooling
isolation).

# Configure
```
./configure --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_0 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle
make -j
```

# Run
```
./run.sh
```
Override the dissipation ceiling (`alpha_max`), the hot particle's
temperature (`hot_particle_temperature_K`), gas density (`gas_density`),
gas particle mass (`gas_mass`), star mass/type (`star_mass`,
`star_type`), resolution level (`level`), run duration and stepping
(`time_end`, `dt_max`, `delta_time`), bulk temperature
(`bulk_temperature_K`), metallicity (`initial_metallicity`), and thread
count (`n_threads`); see `run.sh` for defaults. `run_name=<dir> ./run.sh`
moves a run's outputs into `<dir>`.

# Checking
```
python3 isrf_dissipation_check.py --hot-particle-id $(cat hot_particle_id.txt)
```
`run.sh` runs this automatically. Prints, per snapshot and band, the
sign-closure metrics (`n_neg`, `u_min`, and the ratio `|u_min|/u_plateau`
to that snapshot's peak field away from the hot particle) and the
causal-reach metrics (measured field extent against `c_hyp*(t-t0)` at
three amplitude levels). Gates on two things: the sign-closure ratio
exceeding `--ratio-threshold` (2% by default) on any snapshot in the
run's last third, in either band; and the field exceeding its causal
reach by more than ordinary kernel smearing (`--fail-margin-h`). Produces
a comparison plot (`--output`).
